From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:55:19 -0400
Subject: feat: a pinned tab's x asks before removing it

GitHub issue 50 (pins H29; BACKLOG S-332): the close button on a Space pin
that is not on screen had put it to sleep, like the one on screen, and
removing a pin took the tab menu's Unpin and then a close. Now the pin on
screen shows a minus, which puts it to sleep at its home and keeps it (H3),
and any other Space pin an x that asks first: a bubble at the button,
"Remove this pinned tab?" with Remove and Cancel, Cancel the default, so
Return alone removes nothing. Remove closes the row, both panes of a split,
as a row's close button closes a tab, so the pin goes with it and Reopen
Closed Tab can bring it back. Cmd-W, a middle click and the tab menu keep
H3's rule, and with Cmd-W's setting off the button closes as before.

Why: the owner asked for it, with a confirmation so the user really
confirms a removal.
Removable when: never as a feature; the tab_view.cc and tab_close_button
hunks go if Chromium's vertical tab strip grows its own pinned-tab close
rule.
